nce the cat alternates  between even and odd numbered boxes we  should split up the cases between the  cat being in an even and an odd numbered  box  so let's return to the five boxes case  the cat could start in any of the five  boxes  but let's consider that the cat is in an  even numbered box that would be box two  or box four  on the first day we can check one of the  boxes let's check box two  if you do find the cat you win  otherwise that means the cat must have  been in box four  now that cat will move one box to either  box three or box five  so the next day you check box three  if you do find the cat you win  otherwise you know the cat must have  been in box five  and now the cat is going to move one box  and it's going to end up in box four  so on the third day you can check box  four and you are going to find the cat  for sure  so this strategy works at the cats  started in an even numbered box two or  four  but what if the cat started in an odd  numbered box 1 3 or 5.  well let's see what happens after we  check for 3 days  so we have the cat starting in an odd  numbered  box the cat moves one box at night  so it's going to be in two or four the  next day  from there it's going to move one box  and then it's going to move one more box  so that means on the start of the fourth  day the cat is going to be in box two or  four  in other words on the fourth day the cat  will be in an even numbered box  so now we need to catch a cat that's in  an even numbered box  so our problem reduces to case one that  the cat is in an even numbered box  and now  the problem has reduced to one that  we've already solved to catch the cat we  can now check box 2 then box 3 and then  box 4.  so the whole trick is that we needed to  guess an even numbered box when the cat  is in an even numbered box this makes  the difference between our guess and the  cat's box an even number every single  day so we never miss the cat by just one  box  alternately we could have guessed an odd  numbered box when the cat is in in an  odd numbered box  this also makes a difference between our  guests and the cats box an even number  every single day  remember this when we go to the four box  case which will be much later in the  video  so to summarize  we can solve this problem by first  checking box two then box three and then  box four  this will catch a cat that started in an  even numbered box on day one  we then can repeat this because  this will catch a cat that started in an  odd numbered box which will then be in  an even numbered box by day four  now there are a couple things i want to  mention first there are equivalent  solutions for an odd number of boxes  so the strategy 234 will catch a cat  that starts in an even box on day one  but there's another way you could have  actually done it from the other end you  could have done box four then three then  two  this will also catch a cat that started  in an even numbered box on day one  one of the ways that you can understand  this is that you could imagine the  numbers being in the exact opposite  order  two three four is like catching a cat  with the numbering going from left to  right and four three two is like  catching the same cats if the numbering  goes from right to left so they're  equivalent by the symmetry of the boxes  in the line  so because there are equivalent  solutions for catching a cat in an even  numbered box there are actually four  different ways that we could catch this  cat  we could repeat two three four  we could also do two three four then  four three two we could do four three  two then two three four or we could  repeat four three two  so the solution i'm going to illustrate  in the next version is 234 and then 432  so we search one way and then we reverse  the order  this will also be useful when we  consider an even number of boxes  so first let me illustrate this in a  grid  we have five boxes that we're going to  check over several days  so in this grid i'm going to 